    {
      "id": "f2c047ab5ab90444e45944340d2712a8582ce71e",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 798957309,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Looks good. The current ISO 8601 to nstime function supports omitting the seconds field, so the line that custom handles that case could be removed.\n\nISO 8601 officially supports date times with hours resolution (and even decimal fractions of hours and minutes, which is very rare in practice), so if we add that and add dates without time, we could remove the special handling for those formats as well.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-12-31T15:43:15.009Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-12-31T15:43:15.009Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 133255592,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 5670,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "135ebc001379b57bcea139b22c3451766994ffca",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 798960806,
          "type": null,
          "body": "The other issue is that the no separator ISO 8601 Basic format local time (which we will try by using the AUTO format) is difficult to distinguish from seconds since the Epoch, since both are just numbers, with optional fraction.\n\nWe don't support seconds since the Epoch for time fields for filters, but we might want to later, and a user might think that we do and put in a value expecting it to be interpreted as that.\n\nSo I could be okay with only supporting ISO 8601 times with separators for filters.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-12-31T15:53:53.950Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-12-31T15:53:53.950Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 133255592,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 5670,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "0ed21c209b55ae3a06c658dcdb55f5cee48836b2",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 798964982,
          "type": null,
          "body": "OK, good point. I think it is more interesting to support Epoch time in the display filter than an ISO format that is just numbers.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-12-31T16:09:18.582Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-12-31T16:09:18.582Z",
